ePrettyUrl' => true,\n            'rules' => array(\n                'search-vuz' => 'site/search-vuz',\n\n                '<controller:\\w+>/<id:\\d+>' => '<controller>/view',\n                '<controller:\\w+>/<action:\\w+>/<id:\\d+>' => '<controller>/<action>',\n                '<controller:\\w+>/<action:\\w+>' => '<controller>/<action>',\n            ),\n        ],\n```\n\nWhen I click on pagination links an end of  URL looks like this: `/frontend/web/search-vuz?page=2&per-page=9`\n\nIt is necessary to have a such URL end: `/frontend/web/search-vuz/2/9`\n\nSo I add additional rules:\n\n``` php\n            'rules' => array(\n                 'search-vuz/<page:\\d+>/<per-page>' => 'site/search-vuz', // added\n                 'search-vuz/<page:\\d+>' => 'site/search-vuz', //added\n                'search-vuz' => 'site/search-vuz',\n\n                '<controller:\\w+>/<id:\\d+>' => '<controller>/view',\n                '<controller:\\w+>/<action:\\w+>/<id:\\d+>' => '<controller>/<action>',\n                '<controller:\\w+>/<action:\\w+>' => '<controller>/<action>',\n            ),\n```\n\nAgain I try pagination links and get such URL `/frontend/web/search-vuz/1?per-page=9`\n`per-page` is still here.\nEverything is working If I change `pageSize` parameter name like this:\n\n``` php\n        $pagination = new Pagination(['totalCount' => $vuz->count(), 'pageSize' => 9,\n            'pageSizeParam' => 'n'\n        ]);\n```\n\nAnd rule like this:\n\n``` php\n'search-vuz/<page:\\d+>/<n>' => 'site/search-vuz', \n```\n\nSo the question is - how to use parameters with dashed name in urlManager rule.\n\nDoesn't work:\n\n``` php\n'search-vuz/<page:\\d+>/<per\\-page>' => 'site/search-vuz',\n```\n","closed_by":{"login":"samdark","id":47294,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ3Mjk0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/47294?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/samdark","html_url":"https://github.com/samdark","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/u